# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The folowing environment variables are set in the $shared and docker environments (See ./vscode/settings.json):
#   - PORTAL_API_BASE_URL
#   - OG_KC_BASE_URL
#
# All other environment variables are loaded from the .env file using the $dotenv syntax.
#
# Switch / choose the active environment
#
# 1. Status bar (easiest & most visible)
#    - Look at the bottom-right of VS Code window → you'll see something like
#      REST Client: No Environment or REST Client: local.
#    - Click it → pick from the list (local / staging / prod / No Environment / …).
# 2. Keyboard shortcut:
#    - Ctrl + Alt + E (Windows/Linux)
#    - Cmd + Alt + E (macOS)
# 3. Command Palette:
#    - Ctrl + Shift + P (or Cmd + Shift + P) → type Rest Client: Switch Environment → select one.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@base_url={{PORTAL_API_BASE_URL}}
@client_id={{$dotenv OG_KC_CLIENT_ID}}

# Select the user to authenticate as a Standard Customer, Silver Customer, or Gold Customer:
@username={{$dotenv OG_KC_PORTAL_ADMIN_USERNAME}}
@password={{$dotenv OG_KC_PORTAL_ADMIN_PASSWORD}}
# @username={{$dotenv OG_KC_CUSTOMER_MANAGER_USERNAME}}
# @password={{$dotenv OG_KC_CUSTOMER_MANAGER_PASSWORD}}
# @username={{$dotenv OG_KC_PRODUCT_MANAGER_USERNAME}}
# @password={{$dotenv OG_KC_PRODUCT_MANAGER_PASSWORD}}

@realm={{$dotenv OG_KC_REALM}}
@token_url={{OG_KC_BASE_URL}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token

@sample_customer_id={{$dotenv SAMPLE_CUSTOMER_ID}}


###  1. Password Grant (Resource Owner Password Credentials)
# @name login

POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password
&password={{password}}
&username={{username}}
&client_id={{client_id}}


###
@access_token={{login.response.body.access_token}}


### Reinstate Customer - Invalid data with empty body
POST {{base_url}}/customers/123/reinstate
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}


### Reinstate Customer - Invalid customer id with empty body
POST {{base_url}}/customers/123/reinstate
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{}


### Reinstate Customer - Valid and non-existing customer id
POST {{base_url}}/customers/019c30c3-3c6d-713f-ba21-35286c6f5daa/reinstate
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{}


### Reinstate Customer - Valid and non-existing customer id, with valid body
POST {{base_url}}/customers/019c30c3-3c6d-713f-ba21-35286c6f5daa/reinstate
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "reason": "Reinstating customer after suspension."
}


### Reinstate Customer - Valid and existing customer id with invalid status
POST {{base_url}}/customers/{{sample_customer_id}}/reinstate
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "reason": "Reinstating customer after suspension."
}